From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:37:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: the output of the playing title in the video
 OSD

The output of a video could only be chosen in Settings > Player > Dolby
Vision, for every video and from the next one on. Viewers coming from
the CoreELEC forks expect to switch it while a title plays, from the
video OSD.

The video settings dialog of the OSD gets an "Output mode" list when
the playing video has more than one output here. A Dolby Vision video
offers Dolby Vision, Convert to HDR10, Convert to HDR10+ and Convert to
SDR; an HDR10+ or HDR10 video itself (where Kodi shows it as HDR),
Convert to Dolby Vision and Convert to SDR; an HLG video itself and
Convert to SDR; an SDR video nothing. Each is offered on the terms of
the Output mode setting's list and of the HDR10+ conversion setting:
the display, the connector and the engine have it now.

The choice is the title's alone: SelectOutputSettings applies it over
the latched settings when that title's playback is prepared, and it is
forgotten when playback stops or another title starts. The settings
are not changed. A new signal restarts the title where it is (the
restart StartFailed uses); HDR10 <-> HDR10+ of a Dolby Vision video
switches while it plays, as the HDR10+ fallback does.

Convert to Dolby Vision of an HDR10 video is new: each picture gets
dvvk_hdr10_to_dovi's static metadata, which the SDR output already
uses for HDR10 videos, with the Dolby Vision output, on the HDR10+
conversion's terms. Convert to SDR of a video Kodi shows as HDR uses
the SDR output's existing path for HDR videos.

Nothing changes for a viewer who does not use the list.
